The Hermit of Sallow Fen
[trigger settlement]

FIXME(mundane): PC is lost deep in a trackless rotting fen — black water, biting flies, trail gone under duckweed, navigation by cypress moss and channel current.
FIXME(mundane): Smells smoke before seeing light; rounds a curtain of hanging moss and finds a stilt-shack patched with bark, river-reed, and grey sailcloth; a dugout canoe tethered below; animal bones hung from eaves on sinew.
FIXME(warmth): Cookfire in a ring of river stones on the listing porch; blackened pot steaming something that cuts through the swamp-stink — herbs, root vegetables, something warm.
FIXME(mundane): An old woman sits beside the fire as though she has been waiting; face weathered, white hair threaded with feathers and small bones; eyes pale, clear, amused; three teeth missing; layered mud-stained clothes.
FIXME(warmth): She offers the PC food and warns that the channels will be six feet deep by dark — the tide will drown the way back; the offer is practical, almost cheerful.
FIXME(dread): Her eyes track the PC's pack, boots, and gear with unhurried assessment; she notes she does not get visitors who last.
FIXME(dread): Something massive shifts in the shack behind her — a scrape, a settling weight. She does not look back at it.

